// Cloudflare Workers Builds config for the marketing website (misterr.ai).
//
// The unified Workers Builds runner expects a wrangler config at the repo
// root. Without one it runs `npx wrangler deploy` against the workspace
// root and fails ("application detection logic has been run in the root of
// a workspace"). This file tells Cloudflare:
//   - This is a Pages-style static deploy (pages_build_output_dir).
//   - The build output lives at website/out (where Next.js writes it under
//     `output: 'export'`).
//
// The actual build still needs to run before wrangler can pick up the
// output. We do that via the Deploy command in the Cloudflare project
// settings:
//
//     pnpm --filter @misterr/website build && npx wrangler pages deploy website/out
//
// The Spaces frontend keeps its own `spaces-template/wrangler.jsonc` for its
// independent Pages project; the two don't collide because each Cloudflare
// project has its own `name`.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "misterr",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-05-28",
  "pages_build_output_dir": "./website/out"
}
